# 🐍 Python Quiz v1.3

A terminal‑style GUI quiz that tests your Python knowledge. Neon lights, 3 lives, level progression, and a persistent high score.

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.x-blue?logo=python)
![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-GPLv3-green)
![Platform](https://img.shields.io/badge/Platform-Windows-blue)

---

## ✨ Features

- ✅ 60+ Python questions (balanced by answer letter)
- ✅ 20 questions per round, randomly selected
- ❤️ 3 lives – miss a 4th and it's game over
- 🔥 Level progression – complete 20 questions to advance
- 🏆 Persistent high score (saves to `high_score.json`)
- 🖥️ Standalone `.exe` available – no Python required

---

## 🚀 How to Run

### Option 1 – Run the `.exe` (Windows, no Python required)

1. Download `py_quiz_v1.3.exe` from the **[Releases](https://github.com/jagenheie/Python_quiz/releases)** page.
2. Download `questions.json` from the repo and place it in the **same folder** as the `.exe`.
3. Double‑click `py_quiz_v1.3.exe` – the quiz starts immediately.

### Option 2 – Run from source (any OS with Python)

1. Clone the repo:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/jagenheie/python_quiz.git
   cd quiz
